        "id": 572606486,
        "iid": 4523,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "fix(stack): keep saved branches and merge request targets aligned",
        "description": "## Summary\n\n- Require `glab stack save` to run from the last diff of an existing stack. Reject an earlier or unrelated branch before changing the index, branch, or stack metadata.\n- Reconcile stale targets for tracked open MRs after any required branch push succeeds. Confirm the MR matches the saved URL and source branch, and verify the predecessor is an ancestor before retargeting a later diff. Keep `--skip-push` free of remote writes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced the save bug with real Git branches. Added regression coverage for rejected saves, a valid append, matching and unrelated MRs, and a rejected push.\n- Passed `go test -race ./internal/commands/stack/... ./internal/git`.\n- Passed the configured pre-push hook: build, Go lint, generated docs and code checks, and 293 tests. The hook skipped four optional Markdown tools that were not installed.\n\nCloses #8536.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare and test the patch.",
