      {
        "id": 572510088,
        "iid": 4521,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "refactor(api): inject the HTTP debug writer",
        "description": "## Summary\n\nResolve `GLAB_DEBUG_HTTP` when the CLI factory is created and pass its stderr writer to the API client. Cover clients built directly for login, Docker credential lookup, update checks, and `whatsnew`, so those paths still honor the setting.\n\nThe transport continues to use the existing redaction. The factory test verifies that the setting is captured once, diagnostics go to stderr when enabled, and the authorization value stays redacted. The custom-header test exercises the injected writer through a loopback HTTP server.\n\nCloses https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/issues/7975.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go build ./cmd/glab`\n- `go test ./internal/api ./internal/cmdutils -run 'Test(FactoryHTTPDebugLogsToStderr|DebugTransport)' -count=1`\n- `go test -race ./internal/api ./internal/cmdutils -run '^Test(FactoryHTTPDebugLogsToStderr|DebugTransportIncludesCustomHeaders)$' -count=1`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nPrepared with AI assistance.",
        "state": "opened",
